From: Noahcdls <noahcdls@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The controller only has runtime PM ops, and a peripheral kept
runtime-active (the WCD9385, held for jack detection) keeps it active
through s2idle together with the LPASS macro clocks it uses. Force the
runtime suspend across system sleep, so jack detection keeps working
while awake but the ADSP can release LPASS in s2idle.

Only do this on buses with clock stop. Without it (the WSA881x speaker bus
on SM8250) the runtime resume resets the controller and loses the ports of
any stream still open, so those buses are left as they were. This is the
one difference from kernel-tb321fu 0020, which forces every bus.

Armada 0564 (armada-os/armada 98e87a101559; the clock-stop condition by
virtudude, 50361d799946); also 0808 in ROCKNIX/distribution PR 3636.
---
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 1cbd99f..8534171 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -225,6 +225,7 @@ struct qcom_swrm_ctrl {
 	u32 slave_status;
 	u32 wr_fifo_depth;
 	bool clock_stop_not_supported;
+	bool sleep_suspended;
 	/* Per-Slave SCP_ADDRPAGE1/2 shadow; -1 = unknown. */
 	s16 page1_cache[SDW_MAX_DEVICES + 1];
 	s16 page2_cache[SDW_MAX_DEVICES + 1];
@@ -1909,7 +1910,29 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int __maybe_unused swrm_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	ctrl->sleep_suspended = !ctrl->clock_stop_not_supported;
+	if (!ctrl->sleep_suspended)
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused swrm_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (!ctrl->sleep_suspended)
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
+}
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops swrm_dev_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(swrm_suspend, swrm_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(swrm_runtime_suspend, swrm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
